From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 11 Aug 2026
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix MLD bSTA deauth triggered by neighbor EP reconfig

When an MLD endpoint is actively connected, s_updateEpMldLink() was
scheduling deferred reconfigures (commitNow=false) on all neighbor
links unconditionally. This caused wpa_supplicant to receive a
RECONFIGURE command on a live session, which the kernel interpreted
as a local interface state change and responded with
DEAUTH_LEAVING (Reason 3), tearing down the active MLD connection.

Guard the deferred path: if the EP is already CONNECTED and commitNow
is false (no primary-link change forcing a teardown), skip the
reconfigure. The MLD unit config will be re-evaluated naturally during
the next reconnect cycle, so no state is lost.

The commitNow=true path (triggered when the primary link actually
changes) is left unconditional, as that teardown is intentional.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
+++ b/src/Plugin/wifiGen_mld.c
@@ -339,6 +339,15 @@
     ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pSSID, , ME, "NULL");
     T_EndPoint* pEP = pSSID->ENDP_HOOK;
     ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pEP, , ME, "NULL");
+    /* Skip deferred MLD reconfigures while EP is actively connected to avoid
+     * triggering DEAUTH_LEAVING (Reason 3) via a wpa_supplicant RECONFIGURE
+     * on a live session. commitNow=true is only set when the primary link
+     * actually changes, which is an intentional teardown and must proceed
+     * even when connected. */
+    if(!commitNow && (pEP->connectionStatus == EPCS_CONNECTED)) {
+        SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "skip reconfigure EP %s: EP is connected", pEP->alias);
+        return;
+    }
     SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "reconfigure EP %s (commitNow:%u)", pEP->alias, commitNow);
     pEP->pFA->mfn_wendpoint_setMldUnit(pEP);
     int ret = -1;
